<!--Post: 4064--><!--Time: 1105616595-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4064"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 3:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Could the police have been right with their December suspect? He had to be a very &#34;strong&#34; suspect. This guy was probably investigated back to the day he was born and things must have checked out. The police had to have come up with enough from his past to take to such an extreme approach.  <BR>  <BR>He was a manager at Coleman&#39;s for 29 years and maybe he was not at work on certain days, who knows? He was trained by a group in the military that specialized in training Latin Americans special ops tactics.  The police had to have a LOT to go on to suspect him to the point of a raid on his house and warrant for a DNA sample. The search of his house turned up nothing, no proof, but we know that BTK is one step ahead so why should it surprise anyone that nothing was found?  <BR>  <BR>Something about that guy rubs me the wrong way. He resembles the first composite, he had a brush with the law for trespassing, not a big deal, but still, a typical crime for the stalker type. His DNA didn&#39;t match-- but could it still be him? Maybe the DNA evidence from 30 years ago is too degraded for a good match, maybe he had an accomplice, maybe it did match but not enough points to build a strong case. Maybe the police are still watching this guy. <BR>  <BR>Wouldn&#39;t it be just like BTK to go on TV, look into the camera and file a law suit against the media? Who&#39;s next--the police?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4064-->
<!--Post: 4065--><!--Time: 1105628186-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4065"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 6:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Unsettling, isn&#39;t it? I would really love to have a DNA expert on board here to answer that question. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4065-->
<!--Post: 4069--><!--Time: 1105637262-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4069"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 9:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There&#39;s always the chance, of course, that the guy is innocent, too. I wouldn&#39;t put too much stock in the composite. No DNA match means no conviction. Could the December guy be BTK? Theoretically, yes. I wouldn&#39;t bestow superhuman qualities upon BTK just yet. Dollars to doughnuts the December guy isn&#39;t BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4069-->
<!--Post: 4071--><!--Time: 1105638125-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4071"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Retraction: &#34;No DNA match means no conviction&#34; from above post. Of course he could still be convicted by other means. I&#39;m talking about BTK, not the December guy; December Guy&#39;s DNA non-match satisfies the police, and satisifies me. <BR> <BR>The poster Muskogee is a physician and explains DNA well. She&#39;s also a hottie. Dr. Muskogee, wherefore art thou? Please lend an opinion if you see this.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4071-->
<!--Post: 4428--><!--Time: 1106355398-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4428"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 4:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;They took pictures of much of the home before and after the search, and no damage was done&#34;, Williams said. <BR> <BR>Valadez told The Eagle that he found three football-size holes in his interior walls. <BR> <BR>Williams said &#34;that isn&#39;t true&#34;. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/10697275.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/10697275.htm</a> <BR> <BR>So now we know for sure that Mr. V is a liar besides being a trespasser. I still have many suspicions about him. As far as the January 15th drop, I really didn&#39;t think there would be one as I&#39;d bet Mr. V is under constant surveillance. <BR> <BR>LE didn&#39;t find any evidence in his home because the is none! This guy is smart and was probably expecting a visit. As for the DNA, I still think there many have been a partial match, but nothing that would hold up in court. Besides, even if there was a match--it would only prove that he was there, it would not prove that he murdered anyone. I think LE is taking their time on this one because they now know how to play his game. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4428-->
<!--Post: 4438--><!--Time: 1106362036-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4438"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 6:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think that Dec guy is Btk ..no way, shape or form..BTk wouldn&#39;t be living in a fithy run down house..and police often tear up peoples&#39; homes during raids and lie about it..I know that from similar lawsuits where police have raided the wrong house..and tore up the place..opps..they went to the wrong address...so I hope the guy takes the police and the media to the cleaners like Richard Jewel did in Atlanta...You need to look elsewhere for Btk...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4438-->
<!--Post: 4457--><!--Time: 1106376104-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4457"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Denise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Denise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 10:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree w/ u Essevi, they would not have just went into this man&#39;s house w/out a reason, there had to be SOMETHING there. and yes, i think that is why there was no clue&#39;s left on 15th , he is under heavy surviellance. I noticed that the drawings of BTK, have his left eye, &#40;or was it the r. eye&#41;, well one of his eyes looked funny and , this Valadez guy&#39;s eye had a similiar slant to it. I still think he does have something to do w/ this case. There had to be some kind of concrete evidence for the LE to take the approach that they did. :0&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4457-->
<!--Post: 4458--><!--Time: 1106377101-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4458"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Denise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Denise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 10:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->taken from AMW website:  <BR>  <BR>The 6:00pm news on KAKE TV just disclosed information sent to the media in a letter from WPD Chief Norman Williams.  The letter was intended to defend the actions of the WPD in connection with the arrest of Valadez. <BR> <BR>The most interesting fact that came out of the story was that Valadez&#39;s attorney had requested that the WPD disclose why the focus shifted to his client regarding the BTK case.  The Chief responded to that request by stating that they cannot disclose that information because &#34;it is part of an ONGOING investigation!&#34; <BR> <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4458-->
<!--Post: 4463--><!--Time: 1106389429-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4463"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 2:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Angrywolf, I sure hope he takes them to the cleaners! There is no excuse, and I mean NO EXCUSE for such reckless, unprofessional and hostile behavior by WPD. His DNA doesn&#39;t match of course, but so what? I have &#34;a feeling&#34; about this guy. Is this Russia? Ever heard of the expression &#34;presumed innocence?&#34; Mr. Valadez, start with WPD in your lawsuit. They deserve almost all of the blame for bungling this case from day one. The FBI offered agents and much more money than 15K and WPD turned it down. EGO. &#34;No thanks, FBI, we&#39;re doing a fine job as it is.&#34; Good grief. Thirty-one years and we have NADA. Way to go, WPD! And by the way, I&#39;m a police-friendly conservative. I give money to their charities, wave as they drive by, and everything else. I&#39;m proud to be American and proud to have the First Amendment so I can write something like this. <BR> <BR>Okay, I&#39;m calm now. I apologize for heated words but I&#39;ve had the police called on me when I did <b>nothing</b> wrong. I came within a whisker of going to jail. Fortunately, there were about three hundred witnesses who contradicted my &#40;then&#41; girlfriend&#39;s sick lie that I had stolen her wallet. &#40;I hadn&#39;t been near her that day and had time stamped receipts to prove it&#41;, as well as the aforementioned throng of three hundred. I&#39;m not kidding; four police cars, sirens blaring like whoops from hell, as if this were a bank robbery or something.  <BR> <BR>And no, WPD isn&#39;t &#34;inept.&#34; The problem, at least in large part was, to me, that the 1974 &#40;especially&#41; and the 1977 departments used old-fashioned tactics and had no idea what they were up against. Thing is, when this scenario presents itself, <i>you call for help.</i> Eventually WPD did just this but they did it far too late. Let me ask something, quite calmly. Bear in mind that DNA is more accurate than fingerprints or anything else. &#40;Unless a fingerprint is <i>perfectly</i> recovered, it cannot be used for comparison.&#41; Fingerprint comparison is <i>not</i> science, it is art. It&#39;s art because it relies solely upon subjective interpretation. DNA, on the other hand, is pure science. No risk of human bias or human error. Okay the question. Essevi, and Denise: With all sincerity, can you tell me what would satisfy you; what additional evidence would you like to see re: Mr. Valadez? The strongest evidence extant is DNA but I&#39;d appreciate your input. Finally, as to suing the police/press. Well, have you ever had four State Troopers glaring at you? Calling you names? Treating you as though they were sure you were guilty? Having three hundred onlookers stare at you and whisper? All this happening when you <i>KNOW</i> you haven&#39;t done anything wrong? Hey, three years ago, I would be saying the same things you two are, trust me on that one. I can understand the frustration, the immense frustration any Whichitan must feel. Of course I can&#39;t appreciate the depth of feeling which you two do. The Washington, DC area sniper&#40;s&#41; were caught when sleeping in a rest stop ten miles from where I live. When their target-map was disclosed, a location they were going to hit is only a few miles from me and I&#39;m there on a regular basis, so yes, I can understand fear. <BR> <BR>The police are satisfied Mr. Valadez isn&#39;t BTK because the DNA didn&#39;t match. Do you believe, in your heart of hearts, that if WPD thought this man was BTK they&#39;d just let him walk out? Remember the Manson murders and a guy named William Garretson? Mr. Garretson lived in a quite small sort-of guest house which was, luckily for Garretson, out of view of the killers on the night of the murders of Sharon Tate, Mr. Frykowski, Abagail Folger, Jay Sebring and poor, teenaged Steven Parent, in the wrong place at the wrong time. When the next morning dappled it&#39;s light on Cielo Drive the responding cops found the guest house. They dragged Garretson across the lawn, knocked him down &#34;accidentally&#34; and practically rammed him into one of the now-many police cars at the scene. This was 1969, no DNA. The cops cleared Garretson pretty quickly considering the crimes. Know what they used to clear him with? A polygraph. That&#39;s it, a lie detector test; something not allowed in court in all but one or two states. I believe New Mexico is one of these states, I don&#39;t recall the other. Well, I&#39;m sorry the early part of my post was snippy. It brought back bad memories, but that&#39;s my problem, not yours. Besides, we&#39;re here to catch BTK, so let&#39;s catch him! ;&#41;  -- George <BR> <BR>Tom: If possible can you leave this post up for just twenty-four hours? I want Denise and Essevi to see it. Sometimes a man needs to speak his mind if he sees what appears to be an injustice. I rarely do it but in this case, I felt as though I had to. If you need to reclaim bandwidth, cool. Just asking re: 24 hours. Thanks.  -- George <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4463-->
<!--Post: 4476--><!--Time: 1106403848-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4476"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 6:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi George, I&#39;m sorry that you had a bad experience and it does happen from time to time, but not in this case with Mr. V.  <BR> <BR>Now let me elaborate on my opinion. Firstly, LE did nothing wrong. They were following up on a very solid lead. Isn&#39;t this what we want them to do? Their thinking was to catch the suspect off-guard and find his stash while checking DNA. WHAT IS WRONG WITH THIS APPROACH? <BR> <BR>Had the items been in his home and LE did things your way, Mr. V would have had time to ditch them. <BR> <BR>Second, You said--&#34;The police are satisfied Mr. V isn&#39;t BTK because the DNA didn&#39;t match. Do you believe, in your heart of hearts, that if WPD thought this man was BTK they&#39;d just let him walk out?&#34; <BR> <BR>My answer to that question is &#34;YES&#34;. Without the evidence needed to convict, that is exactly what they HAVE to do. Let him walk, at least for now. <BR>  <BR>I do not feel the least bit sorry for Mr. V. The police are doing their job and this incidence should restore the publics faith that LE does follow-up on leads. <BR> <BR>One more thing--I don&#39;t particularly believe in psychics, but for those who do, Mr. McKenzie stated that BTK had a scar on his cheekbone. So does Mr. V.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4476-->
<!--Post: 4477--><!--Time: 1106406501-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4477"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 7:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One more thing............ <BR> <BR>Why didn&#39;t Mr. V answer the door?????? <BR> <BR>Early the morning of Dec. 1,  <BR> <BR>Detectives repeatedly knocked on the front and back doors, to no avail. Since it was unknown if anyone was inside the house, the detectives decided to monitor the house.  <BR> <BR>Why didn&#39;t Mr. V answer the door?????? <BR> <BR>Early in the evening hours on Dec. 1,  <BR> <BR>Prior to entering the residence, several plainclothes investigators, as well as uniformed personnel, repeatedly knocked on the front, back and sliding doors, verbally identifying themselves repeatedly. Based on surveillance, the investigators believed that the gentleman was inside the house and was refusing to answer the door. <BR> <BR>Again, Why didn&#39;t Mr. V answer the door?????? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4477-->
<!--Post: 4507--><!--Time: 1106449163-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4507"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Denise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Denise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 6:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, I will state my reasoning, again, I think that law enforcement is not going to go through, such a heated situation, unless they have solid evidence. Not, just heresay, especially when they have ALL the evidence items, some that we know nothing of, plus they have the countries best investigators studying that evidence, So, I really think there had to be something there to begin off with. I think that they had to let him go for now, and step back and keep an eye on him.  Now, I am not a super duper, smart investigator, that has access to the file, but that is certainly my opinion....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
