<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4517"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 10:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Essevi: <BR><i>The police had to have come up with enough from his past to take to such an extreme approach.</i> I agree, but an extreme approach for <b>what sort of felonious activity?</b> Iffa, shoulda, coulda, woulda; everyone assumes Mr. V. was subject to police misconduct because the cops thought he was BTK. How close-minded can one get? <BR>How does anyone know that the cops weren&#39;t at Mr Z&#39;s for any of the following, all of which use overkill in terms of police cars, ambulances, fire engines and so forth: A felony drug bust, suspected of arson, suspected of grand theft auto, suspected of aggravated assault &#40;yes, it&#39;s a felony&#41;, attempted arson, armed robbery, attempted armed robbery, malicious endangerment, bomb threats, manufacturing illegal drugs, part  <BR>of a burglery ring, burglary, running a small chop shop for stolen cars, acting as a fence for stolen goods, money laundering, forgery, carjacking, attempted carjacking, possession of illegal explosives, indecent exposure, destruction of private property worth enough to make the crime a felony, lying on the required form for firearm purchase&#40;s&#41;, rape, statutory rape, &#40;it&#39;s a felony&#41;, writing on doctor&#39;s Rx paper to obtain addictive drugs, telephoning a a pharmacy, and claiming to be a doctor&#39;s receptionist or the actual physician, for addictive drugs. I&#39;ll stop at twenty-six. Twenty-six other felonies but by Golly, it doesn&#39;t matter, he&#39;s BTK! I think the obssession with BTK has clouded judgment a bit and rearranged priorities.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
