<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4520"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 11:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Essevi: <BR><i>He was a manager at Coleman&#39;s for 29 years</i> and <font color="0000ff">maybe</font> he was not at work on certain days, <font color="0000ff">who knows? Yes, who knows?</font> He was trained by a group in the military that specialized in training Latin Americans special ops tactics.<font color="0000ff">what years? Seriously, I know someone who could check.</font> The police had to have a LOT to go on to suspect him to the point of a raid on his house and warrant for a DNA sample.<font color="0000ff">Not necessarily; a &#34;six pack&#34; of photos with a correct ID has led to countless felony warrants</font> The search of his house turned up nothing, <b>no proof</b>,<font color="0000ff">this is also referred to as &#34;not guilty&#34;</font> but we know <font color="0000ff">We KNOW?</font> that BTK is one step ahead <font color="0000ff">that&#39;s debatable unless you mean only that he carefully planned his crimes in advance</font> so why should it surprise anyone that nothing was found? <font color="0000ff">Because sadistic serial killers keep more trophies than any other killer type, hide everything extremely well, and of course, the incredible probability that this guy is NOT BTK.</font> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4520-->
<!--Post: 4521--><!--Time: 1106469124-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4521"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 12:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom, unless a few rules are put out there and enforced, this board will resemble your Z board circa 2000, 2001. Just a matter of time.  <BR> <BR>Denise, Essevi, Dpinva &#40;where in VA, I lived there for many a moon?&#41; and anyone else. Are we all here to aid in capturing BTK? I think we are. <BR>Can we please try to get back to this primary, basic concern? Many are confusing criticism of ideas with criticism of an actual person. This will always be a problem because it happens on every message board on the Internet. We can get past this. As for myself, I&#39;m no longer angry at anyone, and the more who register, the merrier. <BR> <BR>I rarely, if ever, start an attack. However, I do react strongly when someone attacks me. &#40;Not an idea or theory, but me personally.&#41; I&#39;m afraid I&#39;ll always be this way. I have to get it out as my ulcerative colitis and esophegeal erosion go into high gear when I try to stuff it internally. <BR>But if not attacked, I&#39;m cool. In fact, right now, I&#39;m seventy percent of the way through a theory which I&#39;ll probably post on Monday. As long as no one attacks <b>me</b> there will never be a problem. I know and agree that computers have become a semi-equivalent of road rage and other anxieties. A quick sentence on a message board to another member is usually kosher but these boards are designed first, last and always for information and pursuit of BTK. <BR> <BR>Example of problem post: <BR>George lists twenty-six other felonies per a discussion. Denise replies with an OMG! a humble urself and a slightly condescinding &#34;if everyone thought the same way..get nowhere.&#34; and the &#34;that&#39;s why it&#39;s called a forum.&#34; NONE of these are harsh but expressions like &#39;ur gonna pop a vein on ur forehead&#39; and &#39;humble urself&#39; aren&#39;t needed to convey the basic thought. My reply had don&#39;t be so ego-driven &#40;all humans have egos so it&#39;s a doubly stupid mistake&#41; and nice try to switch topics. These were also not what I would call harsh but they were unnecessary. Things like that build up.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;m all for starting anew. Only suggestion I have is try to <i>remember</i> to be civil. With practice, it&#39;s not difficult. The post stops here <BR>and please type in your name, in this thread, if you&#39;d like to try my idea of watching the words and phrases we use a little more carefully. It has to be done, or this MB will be a war zone. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m all for starting with a clean slate. Is anyone else?  -- George PS: If it helps, I&#39;ll send you a scan of a photo I have, the picture being snapped when I was thirty-five although I look more like twenty-five. But the handsomness I had is gone and the photo should lend a laugh. I look worse now than I do in the pic, although the pick is not so great. Let&#39;s try to get along or at least be civil. Please? -- George<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4521-->
<!--Post: 4525--><!--Time: 1106478017-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4525"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Denise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Denise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 3:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, listen, I am sooo sorry if you took what I said as an insult, believe me that&#39;s not my persona.I am not the kind of person that is hateful and rude. and I NEVER meant to hurt your feelings. I am not trying to be a kiss butt, but I am sorry if I insulted you in some way. I am not being sarcastic either, but telling you this from the heart. don&#39;t let things get you so down. I wont try and defend my way of thinking nor will I knock yours. ok, lets just let it be left, that different people have different thoughts and when someone doesn&#39;t agree w/ us we dont have to talk til&#39; we&#39;re blue in the face to try and make them think our way. ok? Please, just let it go... BTW, I wont post on this subject again.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4525-->
<!--Post: 4528--><!--Time: 1106488012-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4528"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 5:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The fact of the matter is that LE has cleared the man completely from the BTK investigaton. If they had any reason what so ever in believing he had anything to do with it he would not have been cleared. Do not assume that the only thing that cleared this man was the DNA not matching. I believe it would take more then just that. In the Green River investigation the same kind of thing happened a man was mistakenly taken in for questioning and the media responded with declaring him the killer. That man was hounded for months afterword because he was still under suspicion. The Seattle police did not clear him until that time. Here he was cleared quickly. Take for example the jon benet murder investigation. The parents could not be cleared until recently. No, if they cleared him he ain&#39;t the guy. They would not chance it. The only point you guys are making still bringing this man up in your theorizing is his lawyers that as long has as BTK remains uncaught some people no matter what police say will still look at their client as a suspect. That is unfortuate. And mabye just what BTK was hoping for.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4528-->
<!--Post: 4530--><!--Time: 1106493500-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4530"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Berkeley_street<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Berkeley_street<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 7:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree, but I also think that no matter what LE thinks, they have to have all their ducks in a row so to speak in the event that it ever goes to trial, because guilty or not the suspect will get off on some technicality with the right lawyer. They will find every loop hole LE made and get him aquited if at all possible. LE knows this. Take this arrest for example, he is sueing them. Even though he was quilty of the outstanding warrants, that will not matter, he will still come out on top. &#40;With a chunk of change in his pocket&#41;. People are just looking for a reason to sue someone. And their are always lawyers that are ready and waiting to help you get/share it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4530-->
<!--Post: 4536--><!--Time: 1106503470-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4536"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 10:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->For all those here suggesting that WPD would let a man go free even if hsi DNA matched the BTK, think again. <BR> <BR>Derrick Todd Lee was convicted on DNA alone.  No fingerprints, no eye witnesses, no trace evidence in his vehicles, no mementos found on his person or home.  They had a few tidbits of circumstantial evidence, but that&#39;s it.  DNA alone convicted DTL and DNA alone will convict BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4536-->
<!--Post: 4540--><!--Time: 1106511160-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4540"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 12:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George,  <BR> <BR>I was just pointing out that DNA is a pretty convincing way of being cleared as well as being convicted. BTW, Norfolk.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4540-->
<!--Post: 4548--><!--Time: 1106516303-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4548"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 1:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I keep wondering if its FOR SURE the dna they are trying to match everyone too is btk&#39;s <BR> <BR>what are the sources? <BR>can anyone confirm they have a sample from the killer? <BR> <BR>Did they get it from Bright&#39;s brother who wrestled him?...maybe skin under the nails or something? <BR> <BR>I would put more trust in that as a source as it would mean it was DEFINITELY from the killer, the idea that they would be using samples from unconfirmed &#34;semen&#34; at the oteros seems flawed at best...at least as far as swabbing thousands of people... <BR> <BR>i can see the swabbing/comparing if the dna they are trying to match is for sure. <BR> <BR>but i put less creedence in it if they are trying to match against is &#34;found at the scene&#34; <BR>not really anyway to prove the killer left it.. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>did that make sense? <BR>very tired <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
