<!--Post: 4605--><!--Time: 1106583637-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4605"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 8:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wasn&#39;t expecting so many responses but I&#39;m glad they happened. Thanks everybody!  <BR>Denise: Fair enough. In fact that&#39;s a great approach. Thanks. No more from me on this, either. <BR>Scbenson2001: The mere <u>first sentence</u> of your 1/23/2005 5:46 am post is and was my entire point. Thank you. <BR>Berkeley_street: I understand completely. If police did everything by the book, the guy has no case against them. Especially in no-nonsense Kansas. Thanks. The guy hasn&#39;t won the case yet. <BR>Jrl: <u>Exactly!</u> Thank you. <BR>Dpinva: You are entirely right. My biggest regret is my response to you; I misread your screen name for that of another. A serious &#34;my bad&#34; and thank you. I lived in Annandale but had to move a hundred miles northwest when I started seeing road signs which read &#34;New Houses, as low as $700,000!&#34; and &#34;Houses, nice location, affordable, starting from only $550,000!&#34; My aunt has a house in that old county of mine which is worth over 1.5 million. Must be nice.  <BR>Bodycheck: I hear ya! In fact you&#39;ve given me an idea and yes, your post makes sense. Thanks. <BR>Jrl: As above, very well put. Thank you. <BR> <BR>I just finished the hard copy, in longhand, for a theory I have; nothing major just a few observations. Now I have to translate it to the board, use some HTML, etc. It&#39;s not a lengthy theory at all but HTML is a challenge so it&#39;ll take me several hours, but it&#39;s the only way to learn. Thanks again, everybody! <BR> <BR> <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
