<!--Post: 4790--><!--Time: 1106752511-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4790"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Essevi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Essevi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 7:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, I&#39;m finally convinced that Mr. V is NOT BTK. I believe that BTK, &#34;hand-picked&#34; Mr. V and set him up by dropping enough clues that pointed LE straight to him. Perhaps Mr. V should also file a lawsuit against BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4790-->
<!--Post: 4817--><!--Time: 1106764005-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4817"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 10:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, Wow. I didn&#39;t realize NOVA housing was that high. I think I am thankful I live down here in Tidewater! <BR>No offense taken on your post - its all good.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4817-->
<!--Post: 4908--><!--Time: 1106805222-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4908"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 9:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Essevi - I also think there is a good chance that V was set up by BTK.  But V could get the last laugh - it almost certainly means that BTK knows him from somewhere, and probably well enough to have some kind of grudge - possibly from years ago.  WPD might actually score PR points, avert the lawsuit, and catch BTK if they merely apologized to V, and asked him to help them figure out who had motive to frame him.  Out of the 100 or so people with whom he had memorable run-ins over his life, I&#39;ll bet a few familiar names will pop up, BTK&#39;s among them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4908-->
<!--Post: 5762--><!--Time: 1107358367-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5762"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bluepup<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bluepup<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 7:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Coincidence? There is an absconder named Valdez listed on Kansas Dept. of Corrections website, &#40;and various case dates seem to be within reason if he was a BTK suspect&#41;. His pic also eerily resembles one of the sketches. <BR>Even though the spelling is off &#40;ValAdez&#41;, I just wonder if this may have been one of the reasons WPD felt he was a strong suspect... <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5762-->
<!--Post: 6783--><!--Time: 1108006927-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6783"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 7:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ive often wondered if BTK made the male victims masterbate and leave the semen. did they eliminate them?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
